      "output": "I'll explore the codebase to verify the ticket's claims before writing the plan.\nNow let me look at main.ts, the test file, and the fake harness pattern.\nI have a thorough understanding of the code. Let me check the docs and version.\nI now have everything I need. Let me verify one detail about where the option interfaces live and the version guard, then write the plan.\nConfirmed — the option interfaces both live in `headless-run.ts`, so `types.ts`/`LaunchPlan` need no change. Now writing the plan and sidecars.\nNow the required sidecars. First removing any stale remainder, then creating `ac.json` and `plan-meta-draft.json`:\nPlan and sidecars written. Summary of what I produced:\n\n## Plan: `.plans/AI-3106-eh-run-cwd-flag.md`\n\nThe plan delivers `eh run --cwd <dir>` in **2 tasks**, well within budget (6 authored file-units, 2 tasks).\n\n**Key findings from exploration that shaped the plan:**\n\n1. **`types.ts`/`LaunchPlan` need no change** — the ticket and scope_gate both mentioned `types.ts`, but I verified `HeadlessRunOptions` and `ResolvedHeadlessRunOptions` are both declared *in `headless-run.ts`* (not `types.ts`). `cwd` rides those options objects straight to the `spawn()` call, never touching `LaunchPlan`. I flagged this explicitly so the implementer doesn't waste effort adding a field there.\n\n2. **The \"on stderr\" AC wording conflicts with the codebase contract.** I read the actual behavior: preflight failures throw inside `runHeadless`'s `try/catch`, which normalizes them into a `run.error` NDJSON event + failed `run.completed` on **stdout**, with stderr empty (verified at `headless-run.test.ts:360-378`). The plan follows the established convention over the ticket's literal wording and documents why — the honest read of how the system actually behaves, per the Phase 1 instruction to treat ticket behavioral claims as hypotheses.\n\n3. **`cwd: undefined` is a genuine no-op for `spawn`**, so AC-3 (omitting the flag preserves behavior) is satisfied by construction, with the untouched existing tests as proof.\n\n4. **The `--resume-session` flag is the transcribed reference implementation** (main.ts:139/151 + the options threading), with exact line anchors and the current spawn block quoted verbatim.\n\n**Sidecars:**\n- `.attractor/ac.json` — all 3 ticket acceptance criteria (verbatim), status/evidence null.\n- `.attractor/plan-meta-draft.json` — 2 task titles + 7 File Map entries with change types.\n- Removed a stale `.attractor/plan-remainder.json`? None existed (only `checkpoints/`), so nothing to clean — and none created since the whole ticket fits budget.\n",
