    "ticket.description": "# eh run: add `--cwd <dir>` for the spawned harness\n\n## Problem\n\n`eh run` spawns the harness child with eh's own working directory — `spawn()` in `executePreparedHeadlessPlan` (`src/headless-run.ts` ~line 202) passes no `cwd` option. Orchestrators that run review/worker lanes in per-lane git worktrees must subshell-`cd` before every invocation, which composes badly with scripted dispatch and process supervisors. This is the top ask from the multi-lane code-review orchestration now driving `eh run` (and the same shape an envoy dispatch pipeline will need).\n\n## Context\n\n* Branch from `origin/main` — the local `exquisite-harness-main` checkout is 7 commits behind and missing the approval-defaults work (#42).\n* `LaunchPlan` (`src/types.ts`) has no `cwd` field today; thread the value via `HeadlessRunOptions` → `ResolvedHeadlessRunOptions` the same way `resumeSessionId` is plumbed.\n* Grok's prompt-file handling uses `mkdtemp` under `os.tmpdir()` and is independent of cwd — unaffected.\n* Follow the flag-addition pattern of `--resume-session` (`src/main.ts` `run` command options → `runHeadless`).\n* The `--timeout` and exit-codes tickets touch the same region of `headless-run.ts` (spawn call, signal handlers, exit derivation). Land these serially — suggested order: this ticket, then timeout, then exit codes — rather than in parallel branches.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `eh run` accepts `--cwd <dir>`; the spawned harness child process runs with that directory as its working directory (`spawn(..., { cwd })` in `executePreparedHeadlessPlan`, `src/headless-run.ts`). Proof: subprocess test in `src/headless-run.test.ts` using a fake harness (per the existing `createFakeHarness` pattern) that reports `process.cwd()`.\n- [ ] A nonexistent or non-directory `--cwd` value fails preflight before spawn with a clear error on stderr and a nonzero exit — the child is never spawned against a missing directory. Proof: subprocess tests for both a missing path and a file-not-directory path, asserting the error, the nonzero exit, and that the fake harness was never invoked.\n- [ ] Omitting the flag preserves today's behavior exactly (child inherits eh's cwd); existing headless-run tests stay green unmodified.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n* cwd support for the interactive launcher (`src/launch.ts`) or a config-level default cwd.\n* Any change to Grok's temp prompt-file location.\n\n## Verification\n\n* `pnpm lint:ci`; `bun test src/headless-run.test.ts`; full `pnpm test`.\n* Manual: `printf 'run pwd and print it' | pnpm dev run claude vercel-ai-gateway anthropic/claude-opus-5 --cwd /tmp`.\n* Version bump required (`scripts/check-version-guard.sh --staged`); update README `### Headless runs`, DESIGN.md `Headless execution`, and `docs/qa/eh-cli.md`.\n\n## Delegability\n\n```yaml\ndesign_freedom: low\nverification_strength: high\nsilent_failure_cost: low\ncontext_volatility: low\nrecommended_tier: low\nrecommended_effort: low\n```",
